BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Qi Gong - Mindfulness in Body with Sarah Gion
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T163000
UID:260609-78Qy8fC2UC4knHQ3WUQ7g
DESCRIPTION:In the morning\, we’ll gather in our Ceremonial Circle for a
  healing Qi Gong session led by one of our skilled massage therapists and 
 a long-time Qi Gong practitioner\, Sarah Gion. Rooted in ancient tradition
 \, this practice uses movement\, breath\, meditation and self massage to r
 elax our minds and bodies\, break up stagnation and facilitate the movemen
 t of Qi \\(energy\\) throughout the body to optimize health and cultivate 
 vitality. During this session\, you will learn gentle self-massage techniq
 ues and self-awareness exercises that are both grounding and revitalizing.
  As a result\, you’ll leave deeply refreshed with simple\, powerful tool
 s to enhance your well-being and integrate mindfulness into your daily lif
 e. A short break will be incorporated into the workshop for self-reflectio
 n\, tea and journaling. After the workshop concludes you will enjoy a rela
 xing and nutritious lunch with additional down time outdoors.  Your journ
 ey continues with an afternoon of relaxation\, including a group cedar enz
 yme footbath\, your choice of a massage or facial\, peaceful walking medit
 ation through our bamboo forest\, and guided meditation in our renowned Ja
 panese garden. \n\nABOUT SARAH\n\nSarah Gion has been a Qi Gong and Massag
 e Practitioner since 2003. In her journey to optimize human performance an
 d wellness\, she quickly discovered Qi Gong as a tool for health and longe
 vity. Her passion is empowering others to feel more comfortable in their b
 odies and honoring where they are.  Qi gong can help you access your auth
 entic self and live in a more harmonious flow with your health and the wor
 ld around you. Over the years she has trained with many different teachers
  and styles of Qi gong. Currently\, she trains with Shifu Justin Eggert in
  Santa Rosa\, Shifu Michael Rinaldini in Sebastopol\, and Shifu David Wei 
 in Oakland. She maintains a daily practice and leads a pop-up Qi Gong Park
  Meetup at Ragle Ranch in Sebastopol.  \n\nJoin Us!
URL:https://osmosis.com/event/qi-gong-mindfulness-with-sarah-gion/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
