BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:GVRD Budget - Community Engagement
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T183000
UID:260326VM-8Y0ooc0qFwPXjMig8pw
DESCRIPTION:A whole lot of thought goes into crafting the Greater Vallejo 
 Recreation District's budget each year. We are always trying to answer the
  question: How best to spend public resources to deliver the best parks an
 d recreation opportunities to our residents\, while maintaining the health
  & vitality of the District itself as an organization and service provider
 ? We are in the early stages of budgeting for the 2026/2027 fiscal year\,
  and we want to hear from you\, our residents! It's important to us that 
 we hear from the community we serve.  Your priorities will help  the dis
 trict to make informed decisions during the budget process.\n\nWe've place
 d specific items on the agenda at two upcoming board meetings where we hop
 e folks will show up and share their thoughts\, March 26th and June 11th\,
  but these are not your only options! Those dates are called out as an ear
 ly opportunity to participate and basically the last chance to provide inp
 ut. Residents who can't or don't wish to attend in person are invited to s
 hare using the form below\, at any time! Also\, all Regular Meetings of th
 e Board and the Budget & Finance Committee feature an agenda item for pu
 blic comment\, a perfect place to address the upcoming budget.
LOCATION:GVRD Boardroom
URL:https://www.gvrd.org/operating-budget
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
