SUMMARY:Community Healing & Unity Town Hall
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T180000
UID:26061059uRI2RLrke73AGcxnGczQ
DESCRIPTION:In light of recent events affecting our community\, including 
 the tragic incident near Fairfield High School\, the Solano County Ministe
 rial Alliance \\(SCMA\\) is extending an invitation to attend and particip
 ate in a Community Healing & Unity Town Hall hosted by Dr. William L. Harr
 is IV\, President of the Solano County Ministerial Alliance.\n\nThis gathe
 ring is being organized to provide a safe\, respectful\, solution-focused\
 , and non-political environment where students\, parents\, educators\, fai
 th leaders\, community members\, elected officials\, law enforcement repre
 sentatives\, and civic organizations can come together to listen\, share c
 oncerns\, and discuss constructive paths forward for our community.\n\nThe
  Solano County Ministerial Alliance is a newly formed coalition of pastors
 \, ministers\, and faith leaders representing the diverse cities and commu
 nities throughout Solano County. United by a shared commitment to service\
 , healing\, and community engagement\, SCMA seeks to build stronger partne
 rships that positively impact the lives of our youth and families. Additio
 nal information regarding this organization and its future initiatives wil
 l be shared during a special press conference held in conjunction with the
  Town Hall.
LOCATION:Praise Covenant Church
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1512305830387176/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
