BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pepper on the Run - Beatles & Wings Tribute - Live Music in Downto
 wn SR
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T230000
UID:260605MJtfMt1w8Ee5K2urGK5zAA
DESCRIPTION:Beatles & Wings tribute Pepper On The Run brings the hits\, ha
 rmonies\, and nostalgia to Downtown Santa Rosa.\n\nFrom the first chord of
  "I Saw Her Standing There" to the arena-sized anthems of Wings\, Pepper O
 n The Run delivers an evening packed with some of the most beloved songs e
 ver written.\n\nThis isn't a wig-and-costume tribute act. Pepper On The Ru
 n focuses on what matters most: the music.\n\nFeaturing period-correct ins
 truments\, authentic arrangements\, and a high-energy live show\, the band
  recreates the sound and spirit of The Beatles and Wings while keeping the
  performance fresh\, exciting\, and danceable. Fans have even described th
 em as "Beatles with balls!"\n\nExpect classics from every era\, including 
 favorites from Paul McCartney's Beatles years and the Wings catalog\, alon
 gside many of the songs that defined a generation. Whether you grew up wit
 h these records or discovered them later\, you'll know the words\, you'll 
 sing along\, and you might find yourself dancing like it's 1969.\n\nThe cu
 rrent lineup features Tony Lemieux (vocals\, guitar)\, Ian Luke (drums)\, 
 Stu Dahlquist (guitar\, vocals)\, Gary Schlosberg (keyboards\, vocals)\, a
 nd Chuck Stone (bass).\n\nGather your friends\, grab a drink\, and take a 
 magical mystery tour through one of the greatest songbooks in rock history
 .\n\nSaturday\, June 13 Doors 7:00 PM | Show 8:00 PM Barrel Proof Lounge 5
 01 Mendocino Avenue\, Downtown Santa Rosa Tickets: $10 Advance $15 Door 21
 + Check out **www.BarrelProofLounge.com** for all sorts of good times ahea
 d!
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/pepper-on-the-run-beatles-wings-tribute-l
 ive-music-in-downtown-sr-tickets-1991005252306?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sister Act
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T153000
UID:260604ed57s1ou80m6IpCFTXo6WA
DESCRIPTION:**A Disco Diva\, a Choir in Crisis\, and a Whole Lot of Soul!*
 *\n\n***“One of the season’s happiest surprises.”* —Elisabeth Vinc
 entelli for New York Post**\n\n***Sister Act* is the high-energy musical c
 omedy based on the beloved 1992 film. Featuring an electrifying Alan Menke
 n score infused with disco and gospel beats\, this feel-good show is a cel
 ebration of music\, sisterhood\, and second chances.**\n\n**When disco div
 a Deloris Van Cartier witnesses a crime\, she’s forced into hiding—in 
 a convent! Disguised as a nun\, she transforms the struggling choir with h
 er powerhouse voice\, helping them find their sound while discovering her 
 own. Nominated for five Tony Awards\, *Sister Act* is a joyful\, soul-stir
 ring spectacle that proves music—and a little mischief—can work miracl
 es!**\n\nThursdays\, Fridays & Saturdays @ 7:30pm\, Saturdays and Sundays 
 at 2:00pm Run Time: Two hours\, 30 mins including intermission\n\nThursday
 s Adult $33Fri/Sat Eve Adult $44.95\; Senior $38.95\; Under 18 $31.95Sat/S
 un Matinee Adult $55.95\; Senior $48.95Value seating $37.95\\*All prices i
 nclude fees\n\n(707) 523-4185\n\n**boxoffice@6thstreetplayhouse.com**
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/2025-26/sister-act/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Callie Watts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T000000
UID:260604UDS6Ck_qMUivizifRjJnog
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts is a singer/songwriter from Northern California w
 ho was raised on classical music\, The Beatles and The Beach Boys before d
 iscovering Joni Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy
  Joel\, Carole King\, and all the great writers of the ’60s and 70’s w
 ho have influenced her sound and writing style. After graduating high scho
 ol\, Callie began playing and performing solo\, as well as in local and ba
 y area bands of different genres. She’s played blues with Eric Lindell a
 nd the Reds\, funky soul with Phatty\, and jazz/swing with Savoy Swingers 
 along with many other various projects. Callie has taken turns throughout 
 her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, and lead/backing vocali
 st\, and she’s currently a member of the dynamic Sonoma County funk rock
  band Burrows and Dilbeck\, having joined in 2010 as part of the former ba
 nd Frobeck. Over time\, she’s had the honor of opening for acts such as 
 Bootsy Collins\, Elvin Bishop\, Huey Lewis and The News\, War\, Ozomatli\,
  Bill Champlin\, Booker T\, and the B52s. Callie continues to perform freq
 uently as an acoustic solo artist\, focusing on developing a core audience
