BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bay Area Butterfly Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T160000
UID:260610YaAHm-lqmkKAEsKKHFWynw
DESCRIPTION:What’s happening to California’s butterflies — and why s
 hould we care? Join renowned entomologist Dr. Art Shapiro for a fascinatin
 g and thought-provoking presentation:The State of Butterflies: Decline\, C
 hange\, and A Radical Interpretation of Monarch Decline. Drawing from deca
 des of field research across California\, Dr. Shapiro will explore the dra
 matic changes in butterfly populations\, the decline of Western Monarchs\,
  and what these shifts reveal about climate change\, habitat loss\, and th
 e future of biodiversity. This is a rare opportunity to hear directly from
  one of California’s leading butterfly researchers and gain a deeper und
 erstanding of the environmental changes happening around us. Part of the B
 ay Area Butterfly Festival. Theme: Plant Gardens. Protect Pollinators. Sig
 n up now — seats are limited. To register\, check out the link in our bi
 o page.\n\nPresented by The Vallejo People’s Garden\, The Monarch Milkwe
 ed Project\, and the Solano Resource Conservation District
LOCATION:Vallejo People's Garden
URL:https://www.bayareamonarchs.org/about
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
