BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tails & Trails - a fun Walk/Run for Dogwood Animal Rescue
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T090000
UID:260527LRlI33S4QEOqFUYFwUj4qQ
DESCRIPTION:Join your neighbors for a fun Walk/Run benefiting Dogwood Anim
 al Rescue! Bring your dog or a family member for a 1.5-mile trail walk/run
  in scenic Howarth Park\, Santa Rosa. After crossing the finish line\, cel
 ebrate at Dogwood Village\, where everyone can enjoy a variety of snacks\,
  unique goods/handmade items\, and information dedicated to supporting ani
 mal welfare. Plus\, Dogwood dogs to cuddle and a raffle!\n\nRegister now a
 t: https://ultrasignup.com/register.aspx?did=137912 for this scenic journ
 ey through Howarth Park\, while you support a unique\, non-profit animal-r
 escue organization\, https://dogwoodanimalrescue.org. All dog participants
  will receive a bandana. Only $45 to participate with a portion of every r
 ace fee supporting Dogwood! The trail is accessible to participants of al
 l levels and canine companions.\n\nCan’t physically be there? Choose You
 r Route\, Your Pace. Our Virtual Participation option is the perfect way f
 or you and your pup to support Dogwood Animal Rescue from wherever you are
 .\n\n“Lace up your shoes\, leash up your pups\, and join us on June 14th
 \, at 9 am for a day of fun\, fitness\, and fundraising!” For questions\
 , contact info@WanderingSolesAdventures.com.
LOCATION:Howarth Park
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/4245892548999078
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sundays in the Plaza: Laura & Anton (French Jazz)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T150000
UID:260527Dg_j8ZsZRUSWurm3xbhgCg
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a series of relaxing afternoons in the plaza this 
 summer from 1:00 PM - 3:00 PM. Each week will feature a live music perform
 ance from a local band or performer. Not to be confused with Tuesdays in t
 he Plaza\, this is a great opportunity to bring a picnic\, sit back\, rela
 x and enjoy the melodies.\n\nAbout the music: Laura Weinbach and Anton Pat
 zner of Foxtails Brigade reimagine their indie art-pop sound as an intimat
 e French café–style jazz duo\, blending French chanson\, Golden Era sta
 ndards\, and romantic originals. Having toured internationally and shared 
 stages with artists like Tune-Yards\, Bombino\, and Jane Birkin\, they bri
 ng a refined\, minimalist approach centered on voice\, guitar\, and violin
 .
LOCATION:Healdsburg Plaza
