BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma Valley Pride
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T170000
UID:260515BJi6dgUmHUCuqLpF7j3pTA
DESCRIPTION:Sonoma Valley Pride returns for a full weekend of queer joy\, 
 live entertainment\, community\, and Pride in the heart of Sonoma Valley.\
 n\nThis year’s celebration expands into a three-day Pride weekend\, brin
 ging together music\, drag\, dancing\, local artists\, food\, wine\, commu
 nity organizations\, and LGBTQIA+ visibility across Sonoma. Sonoma Valley 
 Pride is focused on building queer spaces\, creating joyful gathering plac
 es\, and bringing more LGBTQIA+ entertainment and community-centered progr
 amming to the region.\n\nThe weekend kicks off Friday\, June 12\, with **W
 e Rise With Pride**\, Sonoma Valley Pride’s first annual Concert and Dra
 g Show at the historic Sebastiani Theatre. The evening features headliner 
 **J. Graves**\, a queer\, non-binary-led band from Portland known for thei
 r guitar-driven sound\, bold vocals\, and high-energy live performances. B
 lending dance-punk\, post-punk\, and garage rock influences\, J. Graves br
 ings a sound that will appeal to fans of **Yeah Yeah Yeahs** and **The Kil
 ls** — rhythmic\, electric\, and built for the stage. The night also fea
 tures drag from Bay Area legends **Kochina Rude**\, Sonoma County native\,
  host\, and performer\, and **Tila Pia**\, an infamous stunt queen who has
  turned looks from Hawaii to New York.\n\nOn Saturday\, June 13\, the cele
 bration continues with a Pride Dance Party at **The General’s Daughter**
 \, inviting the community to keep the weekend moving with music\, dancing\
 , and celebration.\n\nOn Sunday\, June 14\, Sonoma Valley Pride gathers on
  the historic Sonoma Plaza for a free community Pride Festival featuring l
 ive performances\, speakers\, queer art\, local vendors\, food\, wine\, an
 d community connection. With a bigger stage\, more room to gather\, and ev
 en more ways to celebrate\, the Plaza Festival is designed for friends\, f
 amilies\, chosen families\, locals\, visitors\, and allies to come togethe
 r in the spirit of Pride.\n\nFrom the theatre to the dance floor to the Pl
 aza lawn\, Sonoma Valley Pride weekend is a celebration of queer artistry\
 , visibility\, belonging\, and joy in Sonoma Valley. Come ready to dance\,
  show up\, and be part of what comes next.
LOCATION:Sonoma Plaza
URL:https://www.sonomavalleypride.com/?utm_source=bohemian&utm_medium=soci
 al&utm_campaign=pride-weekend---2026-svp-pride-festival-&utm_content=svp--
 -bohemian
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sebastopol Repair Fair & Clothing Swap!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T160000
UID:260514hEIODUrHD0uBHQaBZJIgjw
DESCRIPTION:Do you have a lamp\, small appliance\, textile\, or bike in ne
 ed of repair?\n\nBring it to the Repair Fair!‍ ‍\n\nVolunteers and spe
 cialized repair professionals will be on-hand to repair\\* your items.  
 We ask that you stay with your item while it's being fixed\, so you can le
 arn tips for future maintenance\, how to shop for repairable goods\, and e
 ven how to repair things yourself!  \n\nElectronics repair and beaded 
 jewelry repair will also be provided at this event.\n\nIf you’d like to 
 bring an item to repair\, please register the item here: https://www.reuse
 alliance.org/rf-reg \\(Pre-registering allows us to prepare for your item!
 \\)\n\nThis is a free public event.\n\nThis event will also include a Clot
 hing Swap. Please bring clothing items and accessories \\(clean and in goo
 d shape\\) to share and bring home something new to you!\n\n\\*We cannot g
 uarantee your item\\(s\\) will be repaired\, depending on the existing dam
 age or breakage\, ability of volunteer fixers\, and availability of materi
 als for repair. Note: we cannot work on microwaves\, repair screens on cel
 l phones/computer devices\, or perform any welding/brazing\, but we are h
 appy to refer you to professionals who can. In addition\, the textile depa
 rtment is not able to perform the following:\n\nReplacing zippers\n\nRepai
 ring shoes\, leather\, or vinyl materials\n\nPerforming alterations \\(mak
 ing garments bigger/smaller\\)\n\nReplacing rivets/grommets\n\nHemming cer
 tain fabrics \\(stretchy fabric\, sleek/luxury fabrics e.g. prom dresses\\
 )\n\nIf you are in need of garment hemming\, we require that you please pi
 n your garment to the desired length before you arrive.\n\nJoin Us!\n\nDoe
 s fixing things sound like a fun way to spend a Sunday afternoon?  Or wan
 t to help out in other ways?  We need you!\n\nEmail volunteer@reuseallian
 ce.org or sign up here: https://www.reusealliance.org/rf-volunteer
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center For the Arts
URL:https://www.reusealliance.org/events/sebastopol-repair-fair
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Slow Journeys (CA State Parks Week)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T170000
UID:260513zE0VlPh400uf-vlQ3ETvqw
DESCRIPTION:Do you enjoy a slow walk in a valley\, breezes\, wil
 dflowers\, the sounds of songbird\, the taste of a Douglas Fir 
 needle or a California Bay leaf\, the aroma of Tarweed\, or wat
 ching wild turkeys and California Quail hunt for seeds and insec
 ts in the grass? Each month (weather permitting) we will explore
  one or two of our three accessible trails-- the Creekside Trai
 l\, the Nature Trail\, and the Meadow trail. Suitable for all l
 evels and a range of mobility\, these Sunday afternoon adventures
  will accommodate people using wheelchairs\, walkers\, canes\, you
 ng children\, parents with babies in strollers\, and those who j
 ust enjoy slow walks in nature that stimulate the five senses. 
 \n\nThis outing is free as part of our Annual California State 
 Parks Week celebration but requires RSVP. Meet at the White Barn
  parking lot. There will be frequent stops and opportunities for
  conversation\, photography\, nature journaling\, wildlife viewing\,
  resting\, etc.\, so bring your nature journal\, camera\, or bin
 oculars if you have them. Wear comfortable shoes\, a hat\, sun 
 protection\, bring water and if desired\, a snack. Space limited
  to 12. Parking fees apply.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/2026spwk-slowjourney
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SugarShuttle: Sugarloaf ↔ Hood Mtn\, Pythian Rd—CA State Parks
  Week
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T110000
UID:260511sW0tRalge0ie-zSWGCi54Q
DESCRIPTION:**How it works**: Every half hour\, our Shuttle will 
 leave from either Sugarloaf Ridge State Park's Visitor Center (ma
 king a brief stop at the Goodspeed parking lot) or Hood Mountai
 n Regional Park’s Pythian Rd parking lot (with a brief stop a
 t the equestrian lot). Make a reservation to ride to the other
  end of the trail and begin your hike\, or hike and ride back
 . We recommend riding first and hiking back to your car afterwa
 rd– no worries about how long you take to finish your adventu
 re. The hike should take 3½ to 4½ hours\; the distance is ab
 out 7.4 miles one-way with approximately 2\,300ft of elevation ga
 in. Bring at least 64 oz of water and sun protection\, as the
  majority of the trail is exposed. \n\nIf you are riding from 
 Sugarloaf\, the Goodspeed lot fills up quickly. If it is full\,
  please park at the main lot and pick up the shuttle at the 
 Visitor Center (you will have to hike a mile back to the main
  lot from the bottom of the canyon/Goodspeed lot). If the Hood
  Mt. Pythian Lot is full\, please park at the Equestrian Lot\,
  by the Hood House\, in Los Guilicos. \n\n**Registration is requ
 ired as there is only space for 5 riders at a time**\, but yo
 u can ride on a space-available basis as well. There is no cha
 rge for the ride\, the $10 reservation fee is refunded on site
  the day of the event\, unless you choose to donate it to kee
 p this service running. **Dogs and bikes are not allowed in the
  shuttle or on Goodspeed Trail** (the State Park portion of the
  hiking route). Parking fees apply.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/2026spwk-satshuttle
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Park Rx—Forest Bathing Walk (CA State Parks Week)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T130000
UID:260511ix8hJ6FQiUSb6VSzNSQwLA
DESCRIPTION:Have you heard about “Shinrin-yoku” or “forest ba
 thing”? Here is an opportunity to take a walk and experience 
 the practice for yourself. Learn techniques to maximize the healt
 h benefits and stress reducing qualities of this walking practice
 . Shinrin-yoku originated in Japan and is gaining popularity in 
 the United States for its documented health benefits. This practi
 ce takes a walk in the woods to another level. A centering and
  calming restorative practice\, it promotes balance and restored 
 vitality through a quality of presence and heightened sensory awa
 reness. Sugarloaf Ridge State Park hosts a Forest Therapy Series
  as part of its Park Rx Program the 4th Sunday of the month 
 (March through November) led by certified Association of Nature a
 nd Forest Therapy (ANFT) practitioners. \n\nWe invite you to join
  us on this therapeutic experience of sights\, sounds\, scents\,
  touch\, and memory. The outing begins at the White Barn and m
 eanders less than one mile from the start point in a reverie o
 f introspection and connection to the natural world. \n\nTickets 
 are free for this outing courtesy of California State Parks Foun
 dation as part of the Annual California State Parks Week celebra
 tion. Wear layers\, comfortable footwear\, bring water\, sun prote
 ction\, and if desired\, a snack or a picnic to enjoy after th
 e event. Parking fees apply. Limited to 12 participants.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/2026spwk-shinrin-yoku
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wendy The Welder & The Mare Island Shipyard Workers - JeanCherie
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T160000
UID:2605118ExRDqtA-0m0M0Usx3TBfA
DESCRIPTION:Mare Island Art Studios is proud to present Wendy the Welder &
  The Mare Island Shipyard Workers\, a powerful new exhibition by artist Je
 anCherie and guest artists honoring the women who helped shape Mare Island
  history during World War II.\n\nAt the heart of the exhibit is Wendy the 
 Welder\, a sculpture inspired by the more than 11\,000 women who built shi
 ps on Mare Island during the war effort. The piece celebrates the strength
 \, resilience\, and lasting impact of these women whose contributions help
 ed shape both local and national history.\n\nJeanCherie\, a Vallejo artist
  and member of Mare Island Art Studios\, created the sculpture as a tribut
 e to the workers of her mother’s generation and the spirit of the Mare I
 sland community. Her vision is to help bring greater recognition to this i
 mportant history through the creation of a future large-scale public sculp
 ture for the Mare Island Core.\n\nJoin us for the Opening Reception: Sunda
 y\, June 7 | 12–4 PM
LOCATION:Mare Island Art Studios
URL:https://mareislandartstudios.com/events/wendy-the-welder-the-mare-isla
 nd-shipyard-workers-jeancherie/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wine Tails Trail at Cuvaison Winery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T170000
UID:260508yjfFZPKe30OE_ERDj4cGIQ
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy a new way to experience Cuvaison with your canine compan
 ion on the Wine Tails Trail. This self-guided vineyard walk winds just und
 er a mile through our Los Carneros estate\, with QR code stops highlightin
 g the history of our vines and winemaking. Guests begin their adventure by
  checking in with our Concierge for a map and orientation before setting o
 ff on the trail.\n\nAfter the walk\, return to the estate and enjoy a seat
 ed tasting of our current release wines\, while your pup relaxes by your s
 ide and enjoys a selection of “Barkuterie.” The Wine Tails Trail is a 
 chance to stretch your legs\, explore the vineyard\, and savor Cuvaison in
  the company of your best friend.\n\nWhen booking this experience\, please
  plan for the dog walk to begin at the time you select. The walk itself av
 erages about 45 minutes\, though you’ll also check in with our Concierge
  before and after\, as well as complete a quick waiver at the start. Your 
 wine tasting will be scheduled 60 minutes after your selected walk time\, 
 allowing a smooth transition from the trail back to your seated experience
 .\n\nGroup Size: Up to 4 guests\, including non-tasters\n\nDuration: Pleas
 e allow 120 minutes for this experience
LOCATION:Cuvaison Experience Salon\, Outdoors Only
URL:https://tewines.com/pages/cuvaison-tastings 
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
