UID:260528ryUR58122E-tvXah2Pqzlg
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 14-19\n\nAbout this Class:\n\nIs your teen thinking about applyin
 g to art school or a college with an art program? Ever wondered what you s
 hould include or what pitfalls to avoid? In this workshop\, portfolio coac
 h and educator Barbara Pollak shows some case studies and general tips for
  making your work stand out and\, more importantly\, tell your story. This
  dynamic course is designed for high school students ready to elevate thei
 r artwork and stand out in the college application process.\n\nQ & A to fo
 llow. Parents are welcome. \n\nThis class is located in the Main Gallery.\
 n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nBarbara Pollak is a San Francisco&ndash\;based f
 ine artist\, curator\, and arts educator who specializes in helping tweens
  and teens develop strong\, concept-driven art portfolios. Since 2016\, sh
 e has focused on fostering creative exploration and personal vision throug
 h her teaching. She has taught Pre-College Drawing and Illustration and At
 elier classes at the California College of the Arts\, along with private w
 orkshops in figure drawing and painting. She holds a BFA in Animation/Film
  from the Rhode Island School of Design and an MA in Arts Education from B
 oston University.\n\nLearn more about Barbara! \\(Below are photos of stud
 ent artwork\\)\n\nwww.freckleshop.com@happypixart
