BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Samba no Pé - First Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T193000
UID:260415Zf0L7uixAE2FDpuZseqbKg
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to feel the rhythm and energy of Rio de Janeiro! Sa
 mba no Pé \\(Samba in the Foot\\) is the captivating solo style of samba
  danced in the streets and at Carnival\, known for its rapid\, intricate f
 ootwork and infectious hip movements.\n\nYou will learn\n\nThe Basic Step:
  You will master the signature quick-quick-slow rhythm that defines Samba 
 no Pé.\n\nArm & Hip Styling: You will learn how to add the authentic flai
 r\, movement\, and energy that makes Brazilian samba so captivating.\n\nTe
 chnique & Posture: You will receive tips on proper body alignment to help 
 you dance longer\, faster\, and more safely.\n\nRhythm & Musicality: You w
 ill learn how to connect your movement directly to the irresistible beat o
 f the bateria \\(the samba drum section\\).\n\nThis class is perfect for a
 nyone looking to connect with the vibrant spirit of Brazil\, improve coord
 ination\, and get a fantastic workout—all while learning the foundationa
 l steps of this iconic dance. No partner or prior dance experience is requ
 ired! Just bring your enthusiasm and comfortable shoes!\n\nDate & Time: Th
 ursdays @6:30PM – 7:30PM\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafae
 l\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allo
 wed.
LOCATION:4140 Redwood Highway #8
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/samba-no-pe
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Broadway Under the Stars - Ain’t Too Proud: The Life and Times o
 f the Temp.
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T220000
UID:260330dQmNhKTktUutap_paVQ8Ag
DESCRIPTION:*Ain’t Too Proud* is the Tony-winning\, electrifying musica
 l that follows The Temptations’ extraordinary journey from the streets o
 f Detroit to the Rock & Roll Hall of Fame. Featuring their signature dance
  moves and unforgettable harmonies\, this musical takes audiences behind t
 he music: how the group formed\, the unprecedented chart-topping success t
 hey achieved (42 Top Ten hits\, 14 #1 singles)\, and the personal and poli
 tical tensions that threatened their unity during a turbulent era in Ameri
 ca.\n\nThis thrilling story of brotherhood\, family loyalty and betrayal i
 s set to the beat of the group’s treasured hits\, including “My Girl\,
 ” “Just My Imagination\,” “Get Ready\,” “Papa Was a Rolling St
 one” and so many more\, with a book by award-winning playwright Dominiqu
 e Morisseau (*Skeleton Crew\, Paradise Blue*) adapted from Williams’s 19
 88 memoir. The New York Times praised the show as\, “Pretty close to pe
 rfect”\, with The Washington Post proclaiming it was “Dazzling and Ele
 ctrifying.”\n\n*Ain’t Too Proud* is presented through special arrange
 ment with Music Theatre International (MTI). All authorized performance ma
 terials are also supplied by MTI. www.mtishows.com\n\n***Music Theatre In
 ternational gives Ain’t Too Proud: The Life and Times of the Temptations
  a PG13 rating. This production is a gritty\, authentic look at the histo
 ry of The Temptations. Parental discretion is advised.***
LOCATION:Sonoma Field of Dreams
URL:https://transcendencetheatre.org/whats-on/aint-too-proud/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
