DESCRIPTION:Step into a world of wonder\, mystery\, and renewal.\n\nCinnab
 ar Theater presents The Secret Garden The Musical\, the beloved story brou
 ght to life with a soaring score and breathtaking storytelling.\n\nOrphane
 d and sent to live with her reclusive uncle in a grand English manor\, you
 ng Mary Lennox discovers a hidden\, neglected garden. As she nurtures it b
 ack to life\, she awakens something magical—not only in the world around
  her\, but in the hearts of those who have long been closed off to hope.\n
 \nThis enchanting adaptation by Marsha Norman and Lucy Simon\, based on th
 e classic novel by Frances Hodgson Burnett\, is a moving tale of healing\,
  transformation\, and the power of nature.\n\nPerformance Dates & Times:\n
 \nJune 12–June 28\, 2026\n\nFridays at 7:30 PM\n\nSaturdays at 7:30 PM\n
 \nSundays at 2:00 PM\n\nLearn more at cinnabartheater.org\n\nLocation:\n\n
 Sonoma State University – Warren Theater \\(Ives Hall\\)\n\n1801 East Co
 tati Ave\, Rohnert Park\, CA 94928\n\nRun Time:\n\nApproximately 2 hours 3
 0 minutes\, including one 15-minute intermission\n\nRecommended For:\n\nAp
 propriate for all ages – perfect for families\n\n⸻\n\nCast:\n\nMary Le
 nnox: Violet Spears\n\nAlternate Mary Lennox: Serena Ridout\n\nColin Crave
 n: Nathanael Koross\n\nAlternate Colin Craven: Joe Schulze\n\nArchibald Cr
 aven: Ben Sasnett\n\nLily: Syona Ayyankeril\n\nRose / Dreamer: Katie Veale
 \n\nMartha: Nicole Stanley\n\nMrs. Medlock: Tika Moon\n\nBen Weatherstaff:
  Jonathan Spencer\n\nDickon: Beckett Hepp\n\nClaire / Dreamer: Natalie Bur
 ton\n\nAlice / Dreamer: Miriam Valencia\n\nMrs. Winthrop / Dreamer: Kathi 
 Brotemarkle\n\nAlbert / Dreamer: David A. Bradbury\n\nMajor Holmes & Shell
 y / Dreamer: Noah Evans\n\nLt. Shaw / Dreamer: Corey Wilson\n\nLt. Wright 
 / Dreamer: Mason Hunt\n\nNeville Craven: Zachary Hasbany\n\n⸻\n\nCreativ
 e Team:\n\nJane Erwin: Director\n\nBrett Strader: Music Director\n\nBridge
 t Codoni: Choreographer\n\nElise Clark: Stage Manager\n\nJohn Sheridan: As
 sistant Stage Manager\n\nRoss Tiffany-Brown: Technical Director\n\nApril G
 eorge: Lighting Designer\n\nMateo Felix: Prop Designer / Co-Sound Designer
 \n\nDonnie Frank: Costume Designer & Hair/Makeup Designer\n\nPeter Crompto
 n: Set Designer\n\nJohn Rustan: Dialect Coach\n\nLaurynn Malilay: Co-Sound
  Designer\n\nDiane Dragone: Executive Director\n\nNathan Cummings: Artisti
 c Director\n\n⸻\n\nGetting to Sonoma State University:\n\nThe Warren The
 ater is located in Ives Hall on the Sonoma State University campus in Rohn
 ert Park. Plan to arrive early to allow time for parking and walking to th
