BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tutti Frutti: The Musical- A Tribute to Little Richard (CONCERT SH
 OW)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260619T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260619T210000
UID:260402NYUZs9yb50CIzIgxXZT3uA
DESCRIPTION:A-wop-babaloo-balop-bam-boom! Tutti Frutti: The Musical – A 
 Tribute to Little Richard (Concert Show) is a high-octane\, 80-minute cele
 bration of the “Architect of Rock ‘n’ Roll.” Following its acclaim
 ed West Coast premiere\, this concert version delivers a fast\, loud\, and
  soulful recreation of Little Richard’s legendary Hollywood performances
 —packed with hits like “Tutti Frutti\,” “Long Tall Sally\,” and 
 “Good Golly Miss Molly.” Starring Emmy\, NAACP\, and Broadway World Aw
 ard-winning performer Dedrick Weathersby\, the show captures the vocal fir
 e and electrifying showmanship that influenced generations.\n\nBacked by a
  powerhouse live band\, this concert experience brings the spirit of the 1
 960s “Club Okeh” era to life with nonstop music and undeniable energy.
  From the creators of Remembering James: The Life and Music of James Brown
 \, this production is both a tribute and a celebration of a groundbreaking
  legacy.\n\nDoors open at 6:45 PM\, show at 7:30 PM—rock ‘n’ roll at
 tire encouraged. Don’t miss your chance to “Rip It Up” with one of m
 usic’s most iconic pioneers.
LOCATION:The California
URL:https://www.caltheatre.com/event-details/tutti-frutti-the-little-richa
 rd-concert-tribute 
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Broadway Under the Stars - Ain’t Too Proud: The Life and Times o
 f the Temp.
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260619T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260619T220000
UID:260330IMapEI3y80e1kGfKG_e73A
DESCRIPTION:*Ain’t Too Proud* is the Tony-winning\, electrifying musica
 l that follows The Temptations’ extraordinary journey from the streets o
 f Detroit to the Rock & Roll Hall of Fame. Featuring their signature dance
  moves and unforgettable harmonies\, this musical takes audiences behind t
 he music: how the group formed\, the unprecedented chart-topping success t
 hey achieved (42 Top Ten hits\, 14 #1 singles)\, and the personal and poli
 tical tensions that threatened their unity during a turbulent era in Ameri
 ca.\n\nThis thrilling story of brotherhood\, family loyalty and betrayal i
 s set to the beat of the group’s treasured hits\, including “My Girl\,
 ” “Just My Imagination\,” “Get Ready\,” “Papa Was a Rolling St
 one” and so many more\, with a book by award-winning playwright Dominiqu
 e Morisseau (*Skeleton Crew\, Paradise Blue*) adapted from Williams’s 19
 88 memoir. The New York Times praised the show as\, “Pretty close to pe
 rfect”\, with The Washington Post proclaiming it was “Dazzling and Ele
 ctrifying.”\n\n*Ain’t Too Proud* is presented through special arrange
 ment with Music Theatre International (MTI). All authorized performance ma
 terials are also supplied by MTI. www.mtishows.com\n\n***Music Theatre In
 ternational gives Ain’t Too Proud: The Life and Times of the Temptations
  a PG13 rating. This production is a gritty\, authentic look at the histo
 ry of The Temptations. Parental discretion is advised.***
LOCATION:Sonoma Field of Dreams
URL:https://transcendencetheatre.org/whats-on/aint-too-proud/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
