BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Solstice Butterflies\, Dragonflies & Wildflowers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T140000
UID:260524c0NTe397HUe6ftE0yINgkg
DESCRIPTION:Join CA Certified Naturalist John Lynch on this 5-mile
  guided nature hike with approximately 800 feet of elevation gai
 n. We'll be looking up rather than down to discover what's flyi
 ng around\, learning a little about creek\, pond\, and meadow ha
 bitats. Our route will explore the Lower Bald Mountain Trail  t
 o look for some summer wildflowers and over to the Vista Trail
  to a small pond/marsh for butterflies and dragonflies with retu
 rn via Meadow Trail and a short over-and-back to the "Butterfly
  Crossing" at Rattlesnake Creek on Hillside Trail. \n\nMeet at t
 he White Barn parking area. Tickets are $10 for general audience
 s\, $5 for students\, youth (12-17 year olds must be accompanied
  by a parent or legal guardian)\, Sugarloaf  members\, Sugarloaf
  or RFO volunteers\, and free for children 7-11. Not recommended
  for children younger than 7. **Tickets day-of on site are $15
  and might not be available** Wear comfortable clothing\, appropr
 iate footwear for rocky/slippery trails\, and sun protection. Brin
 g at least a quart of water\, and if you desire\, a snack\, b
 utterfly or wildflower guides\, or a camera. Parking fees apply.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/johnlynchjune2026
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:History Talks - A Year to Remember
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T113000
UID:260523_MvQdEHebEyNrY4tsbFffA
DESCRIPTION:Long-Time Residents Tell Tales from 1976\n\nHear about our tow
 n 50 years ago from a few people who remember it well. Joanne Taeuffer wil
 l interview long-time residents who share their memories of the economic a
 nd business environment\, the changes in the wine industry\, the foundatio
 n of the Healdsburg Museum and Historical Society\, the high school band a
 nd more. And then we’ll ask audience members to tell their stories from 
 1976.
LOCATION:Healdsburg Plaza Gazebo
URL:https://www.healdsburgmuseum.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lavender Bloom Fest Open Farm Day
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T160000
UID:260523MtQ-XpAVK0-rrwFj39ATIg
DESCRIPTION:Mid-May to mid-July is the time when all the lavender at Bees 
 N Blooms is blooming with bright purple radiance\, and we open the farm to
  the public for Lavender Bloom Fest!\n\nLavender Bloom Fest Field Days: M
 ay 23\, May 30-31\, June 6-7\, June 13-14\, June 20\,\n\nLavender Sunset E
 venings: May\, 29\, June 5\, June 12\, June 19\, June 26\n\nJazz Days: M
 ay 24\, June 21\, and July 12\n\nLavender U-Cut Experience: June 27-28\, 
 July 4-5\, July 11. Note: July 12 is also a U-Cut day\, but is listed unde
 r Jazz Days.\n\nBring the kids\, visit the poultry palace\, play farm bing
 o\, and snap a picture in the giant lavender chair! Shop the Farm Stand an
 d visit the Bees N Blooms Nursery. Sunset evenings are special at Bees N B
 looms. Enjoy the view as the suns shines a golden light on the lavender. E
 njoy dinner with Tacos don Pepe\, then head to the labyrinth to watch the 
 sunset.
LOCATION:Bees N Blooms
URL:https://beesnblooms.com/shop/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:E. Live and Chesta Blake with Velvet Shadows and gamayabreak
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T220000
UID:260521mU765Q5aSkiAG9_ZGHleew
DESCRIPTION:Live music at Brooks Note Winery featuring E. Live and Chesta 
 Blake\, Velvet Shadows\, and DJ gamayabreak.\n\n**E. Live and Chesta Blake
 ** are a retro-styled dance duo playing original music from their vinyl 
 releases on Star Creature Records\, along with creative new takes on 80's 
 classics. \n\n**Velvet Shadows** are long-time friends that formed to ma
 ke fun\, funky versions of their soul favorites. Chelsea handles vocals an
 d bass and Eli plays guitar\, drums\, and produces. \n\n**DJ gamayabreak*
 * is a Santa Rosa based DJ who plays an eclectic mix of psych\, afrobeat\
 , brazillian\, jazz\, funk\, and disco exclusively on vinyl. He has perfor
 med locally at Bloodroot Winery\, Shady Oak Brewing\, and is a regular in 
 the rotation of djs at Glitter and Goth\, a monthly dance club in Santa Ro
 sa.
LOCATION:Brooks Note Winery
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/e-live-and-chesta-blake
 -with-velvet-shadows-and-gamayabreak/18969049/2026-06-20T18
