BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:H&L Live: Dan Martin & The Noma Rocksteady Band
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T153000
UID:260606hP4WmPHh3Ua35h5c9kbdbg
DESCRIPTION:**H&L Live: Dan Martin & the Noma Rocksteady Band**\n\nSpend a
  summer afternoon among the vines with the infectious sounds of Dan Martin
  & the Noma Rocksteady Band. Hailing from Sonoma\, these North Bay favorit
 es bring old-school Rocksteady\, Reggae\, and Ska inspired by the classic 
 Jamaican sounds of the 1960s and early '70s. Voted Best Reggae Band in the
  North Bay by readers of the North Bay Bohemian\, Dan Martin and his 7-pie
 ce band are guaranteed to move your feet and lift your spirits.\n\nThis is
  what our stage was built for: great artists\, beautiful afternoons\, and 
 the Russian River Valley as your backdrop. Bring a blanket\, grab a glass\
 , and settle in for one of those perfect wine country moments.\n\n**What t
 o Know:**\n\n**Admission is free** - just show up and enjoy\n\n**Pizza & C
 hill Red:** Fresh wood-fired pizza paired with our new Chill Red\n\n**Outd
 oor seating** - Lawn and picnic area available (bring blankets encouraged)
 \n\n**All ages welcome** - Family-friendly event\n\n**Wine available** for
  purchase by the glass or bottle\n\nCome for the music\, stay for the pizz
 a\, and remember why Saturdays in Sonoma County are the best.\n\n**Learn m
 ore about the band:** nomarocksteady.com\n\n‍\n\n‍
LOCATION:Hook & Ladder Winery
URL:https://www.hookandladderwinery.com/event/hl-live-dan-martin-noma-rock
 steady-band
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:History Talks - School Days
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T220000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T113000
UID:2606061zAhCOWQf0KeWDCJ424gjg
DESCRIPTION:**Teachers\, Text Books and School Spirit**\n\nSteve Deas\n\nS
 chools have long been institutions of key importance in Healdsburg. Steve 
 Deas will look at the early days of education\, when farm kids got their b
 asic education in one-room country school houses and the Seventh Day Adven
 tist community established a college that sat near the center of town. The
 n he’ll talk about more modern schools and their importance in the commu
 nity. And we’ll ask the audience to share stories of favorite teachers\,
  classroom hijinks and school Spirit.
LOCATION:Healdsburg Plaza Gazebo
URL:https://www.healdsburgmuseum.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
