BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Little Shop of Horrors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T220000
UID:260528tfMU8lKH4keuyZa7Mz2UKA
DESCRIPTION:Howard Ashman and Alan Menken gave the world this camp classic
  in 1982. They based musical \\(loosely\\) on the low-budget 1960 black co
 medy film The Little Shop of Horrors\, with Menken’s score featuring sp
 ectacular music: early 1960s-style rock and roll\, doo-wop\, and early Mot
 own.\n\nThe story centers on meek floral assistant Seymour Krelborn\, who 
 stumbles across a new breed of plant he names “Audrey II” after his co
 worker crush. This foul-mouthed\, R&B-singing carnivore promises unending 
 fame and fortune to the down-and-out Krelborn as long as he keeps feeding 
 it BLOOD. Over time\, though\, Seymour discovers Audrey II’s out-of-this
 -world origins and its intent toward global domination!\n\nJune 26\, 27\, 
 28\; July 2\\*\, 3\, 5\, 9\, 10\, 11\, 12\n\nFriday and Saturday Shows: 7:
 30 PM\n\nSunday Matinee: 2:00 PM\n\n\\*Value Thursday: 7:30 PM\n\nBook and
  Lyrics by Howard Ashman\n\nMusic By Alan Menken  \n\nDirector     
              Katie Watts-Whitaker\n\nMusic Director      
   Kelly Considine\n\nChoreographer       Katie Watts-Whitaker
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/little-shop/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
