BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SPEAKING HORSE Summer: Grow\, Shine\, Align
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T091000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T110000
UID:260610ctHnI81ypUejI2-eZLJ9MQ
DESCRIPTION:Understanding the Nervous Systems of Horses and Humans with He
 art and Mind Equine's rescue herd. Everyone welcome.\n\nSpeaking Horse Cla
 ss is offered by Heart & Mind Equine Rescue. Meet our rescued therapy hor
 ses\, explore our volunteer program\, and learn about holistic horse keepi
 ng and equine-assisted services \\(e.g.\, therapy\, coaching\, leadership\
 , and team building with horses\\). No experience is necessary\, and both 
 horse and mental health professionals are welcome—truly all are welcome 
 \\(ages 9\\+\\).\n\nSUMMER SOLSTICE THEME:\n\nEarly summer and the summer 
 solstice are a sacred invitation to grow\, shine\, and align—both with 
 the rhythms of the Earth and with the unfolding of your own life. The hors
 e herd lives in perpetual alignment through instinct and presence. Humans 
 learn and grow through time spent observing and joining the horses. Come f
 or a gentle exercise of grounding and aligning followed by a fun game of l
 earning from the herd.\n\nCurious about Equine Assisted Services? Speaking
  Horse is not therapy\, but it is an opportunity to get a “taste” of o
 ur work with our equine colleagues since we use some of the same tools and
  exercises in both settings. Come out and meet the herd \\(both humans and
  horses\\) connected with Heart & Mind Equine.\n\nEach month\, the class i
 s centered on a theme such as holistic horse keeping\, equine-assisted lea
 rning\, understanding herd dynamics\, holistic horse care and training\, a
 nd how these all relate to our human journey.\n\nNature or horse lovers\, 
 high achievers living with stress\, spiritual seekers\, highly sensitive p
 eople\, mental health providers\, parents\, and teachers might especially 
 benefit from this class as well as horse owners/riders who hope to improve
  their relationships with their equine partners. \\(Though this work is gr
 eat for dogs as well\, your dogs are not welcome at our horse rescue due t
 o liability and distraction concerns.\\) Newcomers and novices are most we
 lcome. Service dogs do not usually do well at the barn\, but please email 
 to discuss.\n\nCome and experience the magic of working with horses firsth
 and. Get ready to roll up your sleeves\, get your hands dirty\, and connec
 t with these majestic creatures. Whether you're a seasoned equestrian or j
 ust starting out\, there's something for everyone at our Speaking Horse cl
 asses. Don't miss out on this exciting chance to bond with horses and fell
 ow horse lovers. We can't wait to see you there!\n\nChildren 9 and older a
 re welcome with adult participation and supervision \\(and legal guardian 
 signed liability release\\). Youth 15 and older may attend alone with a si
 gned parental permission form. We meet in a pasture which has uneven groun
 d and slippery gravel. For these reasons\, we offer limited accommodation 
 for participants with mobility challenges. \\(We are able to offer some in
 -place\, chair-based experiences\, as well as onsite parking\, so we invit
 e those with challenges to reach out to learn more. Please call to RSVP 41
 5-203-6600\, first come\, first served.\\)\n\nHolistic horse keeping metho
 ds and perspectives form the primary vision for our rescue. This class is 
 a fundraiser for the nonprofit horse rescue\, so please donate what you ca
 n\, either here\, by VenMo\, or at the class. Directions and liability pap
 erwork are sent upon registration. This is a volunteer orientation as well
 . It is an opportunity to meet our herd\, both horses and humans\, and fin
 d out if you might like to get involved. All registration fees are donatio
 ns that support the rescue herd.
LOCATION:Heart and Mind Equine
URL:https://areyouhighlysensitive.thrivecart.com/speaking-horse-summer/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:25th Annual Open Gardens Day Celebration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T160000
UID:260610aoXVdny9y0-ppVD8CSA6tQ
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special day of nature\, learning\, and community
  at Hallberg Butterfly Gardens\, a nonprofit and wildlife sanctuary in Seb
 astopol.\n\nExplore the gardens at your own pace\, featuring butterfly hab
 itat\, native plants\, pollinator gardens\, meadows\, ponds\, and restorat
 ion projects. Meet local conservation organizations\, enjoy educational ex
 hibits\, shop our California native plant sale\, browse books and gifts\, 
 and participate in children's activities designed to inspire the next gene
 ration of environmental stewards.\n\nOpen Gardens Day is Hallberg Butterfl
 y Gardens' largest annual fundraiser\, helping support habitat restoration
 \, environmental education\, and pollinator conservation throughout the ye
 ar.\n\nAdmission is by donation. All ages welcome.
URL:https://hallbergbutterflygardens.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Secret Garden the Musical
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T170000
UID:260610TGJs_dHxYEak_QhgrAquMA
DESCRIPTION:Step into a world of wonder\, mystery\, and renewal.\n\nCinnab
 ar Theater presents The Secret Garden The Musical\, the beloved story brou
 ght to life with a soaring score and breathtaking storytelling.\n\nOrphane
 d and sent to live with her reclusive uncle in a grand English manor\, you
 ng Mary Lennox discovers a hidden\, neglected garden. As she nurtures it b
 ack to life\, she awakens something magical—not only in the world around
  her\, but in the hearts of those who have long been closed off to hope.\n
 \nThis enchanting adaptation by Marsha Norman and Lucy Simon\, based on th
 e classic novel by Frances Hodgson Burnett\, is a moving tale of healing\,
  transformation\, and the power of nature.\n\nPerformance Dates & Times:\n
 \nJune 12–June 28\, 2026\n\nFridays at 7:30 PM\n\nSaturdays at 7:30 PM\n
 \nSundays at 2:00 PM\n\nLearn more at cinnabartheater.org\n\nLocation:\n\n
 Sonoma State University – Warren Theater \\(Ives Hall\\)\n\n1801 East Co
 tati Ave\, Rohnert Park\, CA 94928\n\nRun Time:\n\nApproximately 2 hours 3
 0 minutes\, including one 15-minute intermission\n\nRecommended For:\n\nAp
 propriate for all ages – perfect for families\n\n⸻\n\nCast:\n\nMary Le
 nnox: Violet Spears\n\nAlternate Mary Lennox: Serena Ridout\n\nColin Crave
 n: Nathanael Koross\n\nAlternate Colin Craven: Joe Schulze\n\nArchibald Cr
 aven: Ben Sasnett\n\nLily: Syona Ayyankeril\n\nRose / Dreamer: Katie Veale
 \n\nMartha: Nicole Stanley\n\nMrs. Medlock: Tika Moon\n\nBen Weatherstaff:
  Jonathan Spencer\n\nDickon: Beckett Hepp\n\nClaire / Dreamer: Natalie Bur
 ton\n\nAlice / Dreamer: Miriam Valencia\n\nMrs. Winthrop / Dreamer: Kathi 
 Brotemarkle\n\nAlbert / Dreamer: David A. Bradbury\n\nMajor Holmes & Shell
 y / Dreamer: Noah Evans\n\nLt. Shaw / Dreamer: Corey Wilson\n\nLt. Wright 
 / Dreamer: Mason Hunt\n\nNeville Craven: Zachary Hasbany\n\n⸻\n\nCreativ
 e Team:\n\nJane Erwin: Director\n\nBrett Strader: Music Director\n\nBridge
 t Codoni: Choreographer\n\nElise Clark: Stage Manager\n\nJohn Sheridan: As
 sistant Stage Manager\n\nRoss Tiffany-Brown: Technical Director\n\nApril G
 eorge: Lighting Designer\n\nMateo Felix: Prop Designer / Co-Sound Designer
 \n\nDonnie Frank: Costume Designer & Hair/Makeup Designer\n\nPeter Crompto
 n: Set Designer\n\nJohn Rustan: Dialect Coach\n\nLaurynn Malilay: Co-Sound
  Designer\n\nDiane Dragone: Executive Director\n\nNathan Cummings: Artisti
 c Director\n\n⸻\n\nGetting to Sonoma State University:\n\nThe Warren The
 ater is located in Ives Hall on the Sonoma State University campus in Rohn
 ert Park. Plan to arrive early to allow time for parking and walking to th
 e venue.\n\nhttps://cinnabartheater.org/show/thesecretgarden/
LOCATION:Sonoma State University
URL:https://cinnabartheater.org/show/thesecretgarden/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Abstraction in Mixed Media: Learn to Develop a Powerful Abstract P
 ainting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T150000
UID:2606078YnLunFUWU2DiXXHbLYK-g
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nSunday\, June 28\, 2026 10:00 AM – 3:00 PM\n\nLo
 cation\n\nGallery 212\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nEvent Categorie
 s: Drawing & Painting\, Workshops\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistr
 ation Cost:\n\n$100\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$20\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n
 \n$120\n\nCreate a compelling abstract piece: explore intuition\, layering
 \, balance\, focal points\, and mixed media techniques with bold\, experim
 ental tools.\n\nAbout the Class\n\nThis workshop guides you through the fu
 ll journey of creating a compelling abstract work from start to finish. Yo
 u’ll strengthen your artistic instincts while learning how to build a me
 aningful concept or visual narrative that anchors your piece. We will expl
 ore:\n\nDeveloping intuitive decision-making\n\nBuilding\, adjusting\, and
  refining layers\n\nFinding balance between control and spontaneity\n\nCre
 ating dynamic focal points and luminous highlights\n\nUsing a wide range o
 f mixed media materials — including collage\, paint\, crayons\, oil past
 els\, and unexpected household tools like plastic wrap and Q-tips — you
 ’ll experiment with texture\, mark-making\, and innovative surface techn
 iques. This class is about courage\, curiosity\, and learning how to “wr
 estle” with a painting until it becomes something honest\, layered\, and
  alive. Paints and substrate will be provided through the materials fee. S
 ee the supply list for additional items to bring. Note: There will be a on
 e-hour lunch break. Please bring a bag lunch.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/abstraction-in-mixed-media-
 learn-to-develop-a-powerful-abstract-painting/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:No Cell Sundays: Marcus & Devin
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T143000
UID:260606NqT4C6fiyU2QXr3o8NFpvw
DESCRIPTION:**Soul Meets Keys: Marcus & Devin Live**\n\nJoin us for No Cel
 l Sundays with Marcus & Devin\, a duo that transforms Sunday afternoons in
 to something extraordinary.\n\nMarcus Urani is one of Northern California'
 s most celebrated pianists and keyboardists. Educated in musical theory an
 d an original member of Groundation\, Marcus has toured the world and spen
 t 25+ years composing\, arranging\, producing\, and playing with countless
  musical acts. With mastery across nearly all genres\, Marcus creates rich
  musical landscapes that captivate from the first note.\n\nPaired with voc
 alist and lyricist Devin Ruddick's emotive and soaring vocals\, this duo d
 elivers a one-two punch that captivates without intrusion—adding melodic
  bliss as they cover a catalog of meaningful artists spanning seven decade
 s.\n\n**What's No Cell Sundays?**\n\nIt's simple: disconnect from your dev
 ices\, reconnect with great wine\, live music\, and the people around you.
  *Check your phone with us at the door and receive a complimentary tasting
 .* Bring a blanket\, grab a glass\, and spend your Sunday the way it was m
 eant to be spent.
LOCATION:Hook & Ladder Winery
URL:https://www.hookandladderwinery.com/event/no-cell-sundays-marcus-devin
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Callie Watts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T000000
UID:260604inre3oDFV0OlGr4YfeiEXw
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts is a singer/songwriter from Northern California w
 ho was raised on classical music\, The Beatles and The Beach Boys before d
 iscovering Joni Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy
  Joel\, Carole King\, and all the great writers of the ’60s and 70’s w
 ho have influenced her sound and writing style. After graduating high scho
 ol\, Callie began playing and performing solo\, as well as in local and ba
 y area bands of different genres. She’s played blues with Eric Lindell a
 nd the Reds\, funky soul with Phatty\, and jazz/swing with Savoy Swingers 
 along with many other various projects. Callie has taken turns throughout 
 her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, and lead/backing vocali
 st\, and she’s currently a member of the dynamic Sonoma County funk rock
  band Burrows and Dilbeck\, having joined in 2010 as part of the former ba
 nd Frobeck. Over time\, she’s had the honor of opening for acts such as 
 Bootsy Collins\, Elvin Bishop\, Huey Lewis and The News\, War\, Ozomatli\,
  Bill Champlin\, Booker T\, and the B52s. Callie continues to perform freq
 uently as an acoustic solo artist\, focusing on developing a core audience
  and a buzz for her original material. Come hang out and listen at venues 
 such as Aroma Roasters\, Rincon Valley Tap Room and Bottle Shop\, and Hopm
 onk Tavern.
LOCATION:4th Street cellars
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108021327?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
