BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Max Cortes Y Su Orquesta Salsa\, Cumbia\, Merengue\, Ballads\, Lat
 in Rock & Latin Jazz
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T160000
UID:260602W1Pp8JTsdEKNjMBbd0XMIw
DESCRIPTION:My name is Maximiliano Cortes\, I am leader of Max Cortes Y Su
  Orquesta. I have been playing music since I was 18 years old. I grew up i
 n the San Francisco Mission District and was heavily influenced by Carlos 
 Santana’s band. My interest in playing the Congas\, Bongos\, and Timbale
  drums was a direct result of watching his band perform at the Fillmore We
 st and Winterland venues in SF. I studied with percussionist Louie Romero\
 , who was Willie Colon’s Timbalero\, but mostly self-taught listening an
 d studying numerous recordings throughout the years.  I have performed in 
 various Salsa bands over the years\, as a sideman\, and in 2019 I started 
 my own band. We perform various styles of music including Salsa\, Cumbia\,
  Merengue\, Ballads\, Latin Rock and Latin Jazz. We always aim to please t
 he audience by offering different genres of music. We don’t want anyone 
 to feel “left out”. We perform at different venues in the bay area\, o
 ne highlight being that we were the opening act for headliner Pete Escoved
 o and his Orchestra at the Pittsburg Seafood Festival in 2023. My main mot
 ivation for performing music is to give the audience a chance to put their
  cares behind them and give them a moment in time to appreciate life throu
 gh music and dance.  Food: Gaga's Rollin Diner will be serving up a variet
 y of seafood & steak sandwiches\, various seafood baskets\, ribs\, burgers
 \, sides and much more! Misc: Gate opens at noon. Minors welcome\, kids 12
  and under are free. Well mannered/managed puppy dogs are welcome in the o
 utside venue area. We will have seating for everyone.  Your own comfy fold
 ing chairs are welcome.  \\*You may bring your own water and "light snacks
 ." \\*\\*NO large catering trays\, chafing dishes\, tables\, or other larg
 e party supplies allowed. Must coordinate celebrations with venue. info@vi
 nogodfather.com NO outside alcohol of any kind! TICKETS ARE $20 IF PURCHAS
 ED ONLINE TICKETS ARE $25 IF PURCHASED AT THE DOOR
LOCATION:Vino Godfather Vino Godfather        Vino Godfather   Vino Godfat
 her
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1698404591438347/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Petaluma River Full Moon Paddle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T213000
UID:260306osQZdULObU-Jh4OCV2Quig
DESCRIPTION:Come play on the river at night.\n\nJoin The Floathouse for a 
 magical evening paddle on the Petaluma River—Petaluma’s Longest Park
 —timed to catch the full moon rising over the wetlands just south of dow
 ntown. As twilight fades\, we’ll head out together in Hobie pedal kayaks
  for a relaxed\, guided glide that turns nighttime into playtime.\n\nThese
  pedal-powered kayaks make the journey smooth and easy\, even if there’s
  a breeze or moving tide. We’ll cruise about a mile and a half downriver
  to the perfect moonrise vantage point\, where calm water\, wide skies\, a
 nd glowing reflections set the scene.\n\nThis is a social\, feel-good outd
 oor experience designed for anyone looking for something a little differen
 t to do after dark—part nature\, part adventure\, part pure vibe.\n\n$60
  per person includes everything: • Hobie pedal kayak • PFD and safety 
 lights • Experienced local guide • A memorable\, moonlit river experie
 nce\n\n✨ Easy. Playful. Peaceful. Spend your evening under the full moon
 —on the water.
LOCATION:The Floathouse Petaluma
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/petaluma-river-full-moo
 n-paddle/17974383/2026-06-28T19
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TAKE YOUR TIME: Oil Pintings by Sharon Eisley
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T170000
UID:260529BTxWH0tyTEyW1oOqVLkhLQ
DESCRIPTION:“Take Your Time”\n\nChange and transformation take time. I
 n her newest oil paintings Sharon Eisley explores the time as a process. B
 e it moving through grief\, re-framing your story of self\, or birthing so
 me new creation\, each painting lures you in with beautiful application th
 en holds you in time for a closer examination of our human experience. Eis
 ley's paintings are all inspired by tarot cards and her personal journey. 
 Tarot readings will be offered at the reception by @SymbolWarehouse for an
  optional small donation.\n\nOur guest artist\, Robert Benson\, will be ch
 allenging your eyes to fill in the details with his impressionist watercol
 ors.\n\nThis June 20th reception will be the FINAL art opening for Sebasto
 pol Gallery in its home of almost 20 years! This show may last only throug
 h June 2026\, then move to our new location. Or it may be up through June 
 and July. Either way\, this will be your last chance to come celebrate our
  local\, amazing group of artists at 150 N Main St.. “Take Your Time” 
 is a reminder to our collective to take our time finding and setting up ou
 r new home for all of you. I hope you can all come celebrate all the time 
 and art we shared with you in our lovely gallery.\n\nwww.sharoneisley.com
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Stories of the Light: Between Tide and Tower
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T153000
UID:260611_CmURtcuc0eLXzz3zPXhqw
DESCRIPTION:Step back in time with a National Park Service interpretive ra
 nger dressed in historic lighthouse keeper attire as you explore the legac
 y of the Point Reyes Lighthouse. From the Lighthouse Observation Deck\, yo
 u’ll journey through tales both luminous and shadowed—stories of isola
 tion\, ingenuity\, family life\, and the relentless power of the sea. Look
 ing out over the vast ocean landscape at the edge-of-the-earth\, you’ll 
 see where natural forces meet human determination. Discover how this remot
 e outpost shaped the lives of its keepers\, and how their experiences cont
 inue to illuminate who we are today. This program blends history\, place-b
 ased storytelling\, and breathtaking scenery for visitors seeking a deeper
  understanding of Point Reyes’ maritime heritage. Drop-in anytime betwee
 n 1:30 PM and 3:30 PM. Programs are approximately 15 minutes long and occu
 r on a rolling basis. Make sure to bring layers\, as weather at the Point 
 Reyes Lighthouse can be variable and change quickly.  The Lighthouse Obser
 vation Deck is ADA accessible. ADA parking is available. For more informat
 ion\, please call 415-464-5100
LOCATION:Point Reyes National Seashore
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1342294331103889/1342294344437221/?act
 ive_tab=about
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
