BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Miss Magnolia Beaumont Goes to Provincetown
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260701T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260701T210000
UID:260514PxjUaZL1QESAbLHSM-LLcQ
DESCRIPTION:WEDNESDAY AND THURSDAY\, JULY 1 AND 2 AT 7:30PM A Southern deb
 utante shares a body with a gay New Yorker—comic chaos meets Provincetow
 n magic. When Southern debutante Miss Magnolia Beatrice Devareux Beaumont 
 chokes on a pork rib\, she awakens in the body of a middle-aged\, gay New 
 Yorker—“Master Joseph”—en route to Provincetown for a birthday get
 away. What begins as shock and spirited disagreement turns into an unexpec
 ted journey of shared consciousness\, clashing perspectives\, and surprisi
 ng tenderness. More than a monologue\, Miss Magnolia Beaumont Goes to Prov
 incetown is a witty\, heartfelt solo play exploring identity\, purpose\, a
 nd the magic of Provincetown. Hailed as “rich\, wise\, and deeply human
 ” \\(Backstage\\) and “a fierce and funny fable” \\(Next Magazine\\)
 \, this charming comic fantasy celebrates the beauty of unlikely connectio
 n. LEARN MORE ABOUT JOE AND THE SHOW ON INSTAGRAM https://www.instagram.co
 m/joehutcheson/ TICKETS: PURCHASE IN ADVANCE AND SAVE! Zones A & B ensure 
 a seat. Zone C has limited seating\, plus standing room. Zone A $30 Zone B
  $25 Zone C $20 \\(does not guarantee seating\\) Tickets at the door $30 \
 \(Zone C only\\) Doors open 6:30pm.  Our kitchen serves our All New Menu f
 rom the time doors open until end of intermission. \\(Kitchen available on
 ly at events with 60 or more advance tickets sold\\)
